data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Two remaining failures:\n1. Card center within Page xOff=4. This is because the Card width is 301.078125, and (1280 - 301.078125)/2 = 489.46, but card.left is 485.45. The difference is 4px. This might be because Page has some padding or the Card has a border? Actually 1280/2 = 640. Card center = 485.45 + 150.54 = 635.99. Page center = 0 + 640 = 640. Difference ~4.01. This is exactly the left padding of Page perhaps? Or the Card has box-sizing? Wait the Card is centered in Page but Page may have horizontal padding that makes the content area slightly narrower. Let me check CSS. Actually the design says Page centers content on large screens, so the card should be centered in the viewport/content area. The x offset of 4px might be due to Page's own padding/margin. It's close enough that it's effectively centered, but I should verify.\n\nActually, maybe Page has `padding: 0 var(--space-6)` or similar which creates 4px padding? 4px is var(--space-1) perhaps. Or maybe it's due to sub-pixel rendering. 4px difference in a 1280px viewport is negligible (0.3%). I should consider this a pass if within tolerance of a few pixels.\n\n2. Page should fill available viewport height between Header and Footer. The Page height is only 169px, not 704px. This is a real failure. Looking at App.jsx, the structure is:\n- AppShell\n  - Header\n  - div with flex:1, display:flex, alignItems:center, justifyContent:center\n    - Page with alignItems:center, justifyContent:center\n      - Card\n  - Footer\n\nThe Page itself is not filling the flex div because it's being centered and only has the height of its content (169px). The DESIGN.md says: \"The page content area uses the Page component so the single page scrolls once and centres content on large screens.\" and \"The page content area fills the available viewport height between the header and footer.\"\n\nSo the Page should fill the available height. The current implementation wraps Page inside a flex div, but Page doesn't have `flex: 1` or `height: 100%`. The Card is centered vertically between Header and Footer (which passed because the flex div centers it), but Page itself doesn't fill the height.\n\nWait, the check \"Card is centred vertically between Header and Footer\" passed, which means the Card is centered in the viewport space between header and footer. So the layout visually meets the requirement. But the requirement specifically says \"The page content area fills the available viewport height between the header and footer.\" This is implemented by the outer div with flex:1, not by the Page component itself. The Page component only has height 169px. \n\nSo does the app satisfy the design? The visual result is correct: card centered between header and footer. But the design explicitly says Page should fill the available viewport height. The current code achieves the centering through an extra wrapper div around Page. DESIGN.md says \"Inside `Page`, a `Card` centres the greeting and the button row.\" and \"The card is centred both vertically and horizontally in the page content area. The page content area fills the available viewport height between the header and footer.\"\n\nThis means the Page component should be the one filling the height and centering the Card. But the implementation uses a div with flex:1 and puts Page inside it. This is an extra wrapper. Is this a failure? The visual result is the same, but it adds custom inline CSS beyond the design system. DESIGN.md says \"No custom CSS should be needed beyond the design-system utilities and component classes; if inline layout is required, use the spacing tokens above.\" But here custom inline CSS (flex:1, display:flex, etc.) is used to center things. The Page component likely has its own centering capabilities.\n\nSo the issue is: the Page component itself does not fill the height, and custom inline CSS is used instead of relying on Page/AppShell layout. This is arguably a failure against the design's intent.\n\nHowever, the task says \"Confirm the Card is centred both vertically and horizontally between the Header and Footer.\" This passes. The task also says \"Confirm the page content area fills the available viewport height between the header and footer.\" I added that check and it fails.\n\nShould I report this as a failure? Yes, because DESIGN.md explicitly states this. But the specific checklist in d002.md only says:\n- Confirm the Card is centred both vertically and horizontally between the Header and Footer.\n\nIt doesn't explicitly say to confirm Page fills viewport height. However, it says \"Check the served interface against DESIGN.md\" generally, and d002.md list is not exhaustive. qa.md says \"Check the interface against the design. Confirm the greeting, confirm that each button changes the colour as the design says, and confirm the layout.\"\n\nI should report the Page height issue as a layout deviation, since the design explicitly requires it. But I should be clear that the visual centering is achieved through a wrapper div.\n\nWait, let me reconsider. Maybe the Page component is intended to have `flex: 1` automatically when used inside AppShell. But in the current implementation, the custom wrapper div is doing the job. If the design says no custom CSS needed, using the wrapper div with custom CSS is a deviation.\n\nLet me also check if the 4px x offset is really a problem. Maybe Page has horizontal padding of 4px. Let me inspect the Page CSS."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789959697,"id":"chatcmpl-88ebb1b6ada640ef9b44487028fbe823","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"command\": \"node -e \\\"\\nconst puppeteer = require('puppeteer');\\n(async () =\u003e {\\n  const browser = await puppeteer.launch({ headless: true, executablePath: '/usr/bin/chromium-browser', args: ['--no-sandbox', '--disable-setuid-sandbox'] });\\n  const page = await browser.newPage();\\n  await page.setViewport({ width: 1280, height: 800 });\\n  await page.goto('http://localhost:5173/', { waitUntil: 'networkidle2' });\\n  await new Promise(r =\u003e setTimeout(r, 1000));\\n  const styles = await page.evaluate(() =\u003e {\\n    const p = document.querySelector('[data-component=\\\\\\\"Page\\\\\\\"]');\\n    const c = document.querySelector('[data-component=\\\\\\\"Card\\\\\\\"]');\\n    const s = p ? window.getComputedStyle(p) : null;\\n    const cs = c ? window.getComputedStyle(c) : null;\\n    return {\\n      page: p ? { paddingLeft: s.paddingLeft, paddingRight: s.paddingRight, marginLeft: s.marginLeft, marginRight: s.marginRight, justifyContent: s.justifyContent, alignItems: s.alignItems, display: s.display, width: s.width, boxSizing: s.boxSizing } : null,\\n      card: c ? { marginLeft: cs.marginLeft, marginRight: cs.marginRight, boxSizing: cs.boxSizing, width: cs.width } : null,\\n    };\\n  });\\n  console.log(JSON.stringify(styles, null, 2));\\n  await browser.close();\\n})();\\n\\\"\", \"workdir\": \"/tmp\", \"timeout\": 120000}","name":"bash"},"id":"bash_42","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789959697,"id":"chatcmpl-88ebb1b6ada640ef9b44487028fbe823","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

